{"Title":"An Act relative to the tracking of medical malpractice cases ","BillNumber":"S1123","DocketNumber":"SD91","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T14:41:02.31"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T14:41:02.31"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1123/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Tarr, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1123) of Bruce E. Tarr for legislation relative to the tracking of medical malpractice cases.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Notwithstanding any general or special to the contrary the administrator of the trial court shall develop and implement  a system to track and categorize any civil action malpractice, error or mistake against a provider of health care. Annually by December 31 the administrator of the trial court shall submit the number of any civil action malpractice, error or mistake against a provider of health care to the clerks of the house and senate and the joint committee on the judiciary.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}